      "Sidebar Issues",
      0,
      "default",
      true,
      false,
      "2026-07-31T11:28:33Z",
      "Page category shows up on the side bar as a page and the pages themselves show up above both the post and the pages section at the top of the side part with no header.\n\nThis would look fine if there was a header on the side bar at the top but it's currently just blank and it's a weird looking empty space. You should at least put something like Navigation, or ManagementCMS using #DE2626 on sidebar header space.",
      "#fce7f3"
    ],
    [
      "note",
      null,
      "de6c63bc-2e2b-497f-9757-c4ca4f5552a7",
      "c24841b1-1bc9-441d-af02-3341d0c1782b",
      "Style Settings",
      0,
      "default",
      true,
      false,
      "2026-07-31T11:40:25Z",
      "PRIORITY: LOW\n\nIn the settings I can change the background of the exported sites background and accent.\n\nThe way I see it is that it's either all or nothing. You got three.\n\n1. Remove these setting altogether... Which which is my least preferred option.\n\n2. Go all out crete a sub tab switcher at the top of the Admin Dashboard settings, add style tab and allow me to customize page fonts and backgrounds, cards, card backgrounds, card fonts, links, link active, link hover, sidebar background, sidebar fonts, list fonts, header fonts etc.... with a save theme option in a combo boxes which custom teams. \n\n3. Go all out crete a sub tab switcher at the top of the Admin Dashboard settings, Add a style sheet switcher, to create style sheet option which would call it from a template and register it in a combo box to the select and allow you to build custom style sheets.\n\nPersonally I prefer option two. But allowing me to change two colors is just stupid.",
      "#fce7f3"
    ],
    [
      "note",
      null,
      "de6c63bc-2e2b-497f-9757-c4ca4f5552a7",
      "2255c9ae-e419-42f8-a03e-ecd9b9899ef1",
